  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CHIMPANZEE CONSERVATION IN THE MOYEN-BAFING AND BADIAR LANDSCAPE, GUINEA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SUPPORT THE STRENGTHENING OF HABITAT CONNECTIVITY BETWEEN THE MOYEN-BAFING AND BADIAR NATIONAL PARKS TO IMPROVE CONDITIONS FOR WEST AFRICAN CHIMPANZEES BY: (1) INCREASING INVOLVEMENT OF LOCAL POPULATIONS IN THE SUSTAINABLE MANAGEMENT OF NATURAL RESOURCES COMMUNICATIONS, STRENGTHENING LOCAL GOVERNANCE STRUCTURES, AND IMPLEMENTING PARTICIPATIVE CORRIDOR BOUNDARY IDENTIFICATION AND (2) RESTORING HABITAT CONNECTIVITY BETWEEN IDENTIFIED CHIMPANZEE HOTSPOTS IN THE MOYEN-BAFING AND BADIAR NATIONAL PARKS LANDSCAPE THROUGH CAMERA-TRAP MONITORING OF CHIMPANZEES, ESTABLISHING LAND COVER AND LAND USE BASELINE DATA, REHABILITATING KEY FOREST HABITATS THROUGH NATURAL REGENERATION, AND ESTABLISHING FIREBREAKS AND A FIRE MANAGEMENT PLAN TO ACCELERATE THE REESTABLISHMENT OF DEGRADED HABITAT.</narrative>
  </description>
